WEBVTT

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.740
That's absurd!

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.870
Sorry, but please leave us alone.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.510
I'm glad there's nothing wrong with you, Nai-chan.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.890
Can I go where Karoku is?

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.470
At the moment, Hirato is having a meeting for the mission.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.310
Wait just a little longer.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:04.190
Mm-hmm.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.480
Thank you.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.610
Then, take a rest here first.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:13.690
Yogi.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.200
The Niji's Promise
Score 12

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.580
What does it mean to be “a child of the Second Ship”?

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.120
What?

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.950
That damned four-eyes asked me if I wanted to become one.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.540
But I don't know what he means by that.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.340
<i>A child of the Second Ship...</i>

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.460
<i>In other words...</i>

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:40.050
Um... sorry, I don't really know.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.140
Karoku, please wait for me.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:51.690
Like you say, I can't deny the
possibility of this being a trap.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.490
Even if it is a trap, those guys who have kept their guard so tight,

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.440
have created an opening for us.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.780
If we take the bait, we might be able to make some progress.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:05.120
The mansion where an associate of Lindain Group had disappeared,

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.040
is the same mansion where Tsukumo was held captive.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.170
According to Tsukumo's report,

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.710
the granddaughter of Palnedo, Erisyuka, was at that mansion.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.390
We also have information that she's associated with Karoku

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.430
from Yanari, the son of the president of Lindain.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:28.100
Moreover, Karoku was telling Nai to go to the Smoky Mansion.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.520
If that's the case, we should report to the Consulate Tower and receive permiss–

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.280
We'll lose our leads if we wait.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.860
It'd be too late by the time we get an approval.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:45.160
If in fact it really is an S.O.S. from Karoku, if we ignore it,

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.460
the keys to uncovering the mystery behind Karoku and the birth of Nai,

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.420
together with the analysis of Karoku's notebook,

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.870
will forever disappear into darkness.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:58.380
It would be frustrating to let all the data you've collected go to waste, right?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.340
That's right. So, please help us out, Akari-chan.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.270
We will send a small team to ambush them tomorrow.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:11.850
Very well.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.820
Just as we expected.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.690
But, I have one condition:

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.190
You'll have to take me along.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:23.070
It's possible that a portion of the data retrieved at
the site may not be brought back in its initial condition,

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.790
so I would definitely want you to come with us.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.540
Didn't you come here to talk to me?

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.550
When will the assault on the Smoky Mansion commence?

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.640
I can't reveal details of a mission to a civilian

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.510
before it's announced.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.560
Is that all?

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.150
<i>I'm of no use to them anyway.</i>

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:56.520
<i>I can't remain here like this.</i>

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:01.910
How long should I stay here?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.080
Nai's been getting along with everyone just fine,

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:09.080
so there's no reason for me to be here anymore.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:13.200
In other words, you wish to leave the ship?

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:19.800
<i>I don't plan on staying here any longer
embarrassing myself and being a burden to everyone.</i>

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.170
<i>It's the first time I've felt that</i>

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.220
<i>not being able to feel proud of myself can be so annoying.</i>

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.100
That's right.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.480
All right. I understand.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.730
I will work on fulfilling your request.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.310
Sure.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.560
Do you want to go to the Smoky Mansion?

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.280
What? Can I?

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.320
Then I'll go.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.570
Make yourself useful.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.670
<i>Is he really leaving the Second Ship?</i>

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:05.300
Our target, the property of Palnedo, the CEO of Gald Company, Smoky Mansion.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.260
The mission is to rescue Karoku who's inside the building,

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.340
along with discovering and seizing of any evidence related to Kafka...

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.270
and detaining any key personnel related.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:14.350
Confirm your roles in the mission.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.810
Make your final preparations and stand by.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:24.700
My goodness, you're pathetic to be scared of a mere injection.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:30.620
<i>It's not the injection, but Akari-sensei at close range that I'm scared of.</i>

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:35.620
Excuse me, why did you come all the way here today?

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.590
I'm here in order to accompany the team to the Smoky Mansion.

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:43.380
Huh? You're coming with us?

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.130
With my presence, the chances of you guys surviving will increase remarkably,

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.140
but I won't be able to ease the injuries caused through emergency treatment.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.640
So make sure you don't mess up.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.390
No...

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.360
As we expected, there was a transmission to an unknown location from the Second Ship.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.530
Were they jamming it?

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:04.820
Don't worry.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.030
It was blocked completely.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:15.250
Everyone, equip your bracelets.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.250
Confirm that it's locked.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.000
Hand in raised position.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.250
Activation test.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.720
Keep in mind of your partner's actions,

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:33.220
prepare to fight using your own intuition.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:37.730
<i>Karoku.</i>

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:45.570
Nai.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.570
There's someone named Karoku here, isn't there?

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:52.580
I'm his buddy.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:55.830
He contacted me to rescue him
because he's being held captive.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:56.500
What?

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.830
I'm sorry.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.420
This kid begged me so profusely,

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:04.710
so I brought him here to satisfy his request.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.840
Sorry, I haven't introduced myself.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.430
I am from the National Defense Organization, Circus,

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.840
the Second Ship Fighter, Yogi.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.810
There's no one like that here.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:17.060
There must be some kind of mistake.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.270
Of course you would say that.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.600
But that's just a lie!

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.230
Karoku!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.190
Hey!
Hey you!

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.860
I'm sorry, I'll bring him back right away!

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:26.400
Stop!
I'm sorry, I'll bring him back right away!

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.990
Contact the mansion!

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:33.120
When I first heard it, I was stunned how childish the plan was.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.530
It's intentional.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:38.200
If they pretend to be an innocent organization,

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.540
they would be hesitant to create any bloodshed

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.620
at the front gate which connects to the ordinary world.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.500
What's the problem?

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.340
Yes, sir.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:52.260
Well, some random guy said Karoku-sama had asked for help and then...

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.760
Don't panic.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.100
There's no problem.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.760
But find him,

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.560
and take care of things properly.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.150
<i>Circus...</i>

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:05.820
<i>I don't know what made them so confident to come here,</i>

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.650
<i>but this place can never be revealed by mere humans.</i>

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:14.610
<i>Let them enjoy guessing what's truly hiding inside the box.</i>

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.830
<i> It's the job of humans to use their imagination. </i>

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:27.170
<i>And ours, to create and make it a reality. </i>

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.260
Gareki-kun!

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.380
We're flying up.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.180
What's that thing you're looking at?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.930
I stole it from the man at the front gate.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.430
What? Back there?

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:45.190
I thought it might have a rough sketch of the premises.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.400
Karoku!

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:55.620
Uro is asking you to return to your room.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:57.530
Did something happen?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.200
I'm not sure.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.450
But I don't really care,

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.290
because I'm with you.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:12.970
The skies roared and the wind has risen.

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:13.930
What?

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.050
It'll be raining soon, so let's go inside.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.260
It appears that someone is here to see me.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:24.350
Karoku?

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.520
My special child.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:35.200
Good. I've disabled the main security system.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.190
It should help to keep the guards off our backs for the time being.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.460
Gareki-kun, you're amazing.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:51.420
You're always studying by reading difficult books, aren't you?

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:57.640
Is it because... you want to go into that line of work in the future?

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:58.430
Well...

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.680
There's a job like that in Circus too...

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.890
What? "Studying," you say?

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.480
It just helps me get a living.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.110
I've obtained control over the system.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:11.980
I'll connect it to the Second Ship now.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:12.610
Yogi.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:14.320
Ah, okay.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:15.740
First of all, this button...

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:17.320
No, the one below.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:17.900
What?

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.910
Next, the right one.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.240
Then, the one on the bottom left!

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.410
The side switch... lift it up!

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.630
The security's been turned off!

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:29.580
What the hell happened?!

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.960
We have complete control over the network.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:37.460
Go.

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:49.480
We are the National Defense Organization, Circus.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:54.650
Everyone, stay where you are and follow our orders.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.740
Come, let's go treasure hunting.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:02.660
With your ears, sift through the sounds of monsters and treasures being moved around.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:09.460
If you can't find him, you may never see Gareki-kun again.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:14.090
Why are you having so much trouble with a mere organization like Circus?!

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.010
They took control of the network.

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:16.630
Huh?

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.800
Our data's leaking out!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:30.680
Gareki-kun, outside!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.200
Let's see.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:45.860
Since they're dancing for us, I should welcome them with applause.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.740
With a rhythm so loud that it will never leave their ears.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.090
I hear a loud sound.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.880
The enemy has finally showed their true colors.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:01.710
Here they come!

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:03.880
Everyone, to victory!

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.190
Gareki-kun!

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:18.940
Him again...

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.990
Are they trying to destroy the entire mansion?

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.160
We must hurry!

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:37.090
Kiichi, I'll leave you to take care of things here!

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.460
Okay!

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:41.010
Hey Kiharu, he's getting away!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:46.380
I'll be your opponent!

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:50.390
The girls in Circus are all pretty cute, huh?

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:53.600
You'll realize that I'm much more than just <i>cute</i>!

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:59.820
Open up, Karoku! You're inside, aren't you?

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:02.820
Erisyuka-sama, we should be going soon.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.320
No! I won't go unless Karoku is coming with me!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.030
We can't stay! Circus is on their way here!

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.280
Circus?

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.700
<i>It appears that someone is here to see me.</i>

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.200
<i>My special child.</i>

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:21.210
So that girl is coming...

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.720
To see Karoku again?

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.260
Does she love Karoku?

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:28.090
No! I don't want that!

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:29.470
I won't allow them to meet!

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:34.190
Uro, that girl from Circus is coming for Karoku, right?

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.020
I'll never let them mee–

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:04.380
<i>Crate of Thorns!</i>

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:19.610
<i>If he wasn't around,</i>

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:23.480
<i>I... would definitely have died!</i>

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:30.030
<i>I must listen closely!</i>

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:32.490
<i>Karoku had said he's here!</i>

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:40.290
Oh, sorry I laughed at you.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.670
But you were behaving just like a little animal...

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:51.970
Nai-kun, I'll become your eyes.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:55.680
So close them and concentrate on listening.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:03.730
Uro, don't let that girl and Karoku see each other!

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.490
Your wish is my command.

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:08.980
I'll toy with these women from Circus until they die.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.240
Set your mind at rest.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:13.860
Huh?

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:21.370
Greetings, lovely goddesses of Circus.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.750
You're Uro-san, aren't you?

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.000
Thanks for personally coming to greet us.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:30.720
It seems like a considerable amount of <i>things</i> have been removed from the building.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.130
What's the present situation?

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.140
Let's see...

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:38.270
Everything has pretty much been neatly tidied up,

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:42.640
but we didn't come here for a cleaning inspection.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:44.520
Well then, wha–

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.860
How admirable, you didn't dodge at all.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.030
You're pretty well-trained, aren't you?

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.790
I'm right, aren't I?

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:58.960
Normal human beings wouldn't be able to avoid a Circus member's attack,

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:03.160
nor land on the ground unharmed after falling such a distance.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:07.670
You're under arrest as a level 6 member of Kafka!

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:14.550
I'll be right back.

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.850
Hello. It's been a long time.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:23.690
You know, right now Nai is coming to see me.

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:26.610
How would you like to come along?

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:30.320
As sparkling stars descend,

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.780
the little lamb learns of the sky.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:37.450
The Second Ship Fighter of the National Defense Organization, Circus, Tsukumo!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.950
As well as Iva!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.580
Here we come!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:01.350
<i>Willfulness of the Constellations!</i>

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:16.780
Die.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:34.960
Sensei, exactly what do we achieve from doing this?

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:38.880
What the hell are you doing?!

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:41.930
Sensei...

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:47.150
The more I think about it, the more I don't understand.

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:52.940
Varuga are superior beings that threaten our very existence, are they not??

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:55.230
Even Circus members have a hard time dealing with them,

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:58.110
and have so far failed to suppress the activities of Kafka.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.830
I couldn't stop trying to figure out why we've been losing,

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:05.790
even when we're supposedly doing things that are right.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.880
It hurts so much thinking about it constantly.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.460
I thought over, and over, and over again.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.210
And it finally came to me...

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:16.340
I figured that they're strong because <i>they're</i> the ones on the right side of justice.

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:18.340
Azana!

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:25.690
We didn't notice that because we're inferior lifeforms to them.

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:27.850
We just couldn't see the truth.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.190
We had lost sight of it!

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:31.480
Wh-What are you say–

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:32.940
Akari-sensei.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:35.650
You possess wonderful capabilities.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:39.450
They would certainly accept you as one of them.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:42.740
Azana... You...

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.240
<i>Joyful Blindness.</i>

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.550
Jiki-kun...

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:57.340
Nai-kun, just focus.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.220
Mr. Sheep!

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:04.680
Mr. Sheep! Mr. Sheep!

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:06.810
The sheep are just mere machines.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:09.270
A new one can always be made.

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:12.940
We played together...

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:17.900
You wouldn't know if that's the same sheep, right?

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:21.120
There's so many of them, and every one of them looks the same.

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:23.740
But Jiki-kun...

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:26.910
Out of those I've met so far...

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:29.040
None of them had been the same.

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:35.340
Mr. Flower and the other Mr. Flower...

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.130
They were different.

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:52.600
If Karoku dies, it means he'll be gone forever.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.690
I must find him.

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:58.610
Everyone...

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:17.500
The sky told me it was going to rain,

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:24.930
and the little ones told me that lots of flowers had bloomed.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:28.890
That's right...

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:35.110
My voice will also reach far away!

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:02.800
<i>Sapphire Crown!</i>

00:22:22.990 --> 00:22:25.360
I'm surprised that you've lasted this long.

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:26.870
I respect you for that.

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:31.660
But the difference between our abilities is far too great to begin with.

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:37.460
Is the Second Ship Captain hiding in his ship?

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:40.340
I can't believe he's just sitting back and watching the battle.

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:42.630
He should not only give instructions, but get his ass do–

00:22:43.930 --> 00:22:44.630
What?!

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:48.430
Impossible! The gate shouldn't have been opened...

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:51.010
Banshees?

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:00.190
Our leader wishes to capture you alive.

00:23:00.570 --> 00:23:04.360
I was having a really hard time holding back, you know?

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:13.250
What's that?

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.340
Gareki-kun, what's wrong?

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:30.760
Why are you letting out such a deep sigh as if you've lost all hope?

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:32.350
What happened? Tell me! Okay?

00:23:32.350 --> 00:23:34.020
If you have any problems, tell me all about it.

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:34.770
Got it? Okay?

00:23:34.770 --> 00:23:35.730
I'll definitely help you!

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:36.680
Can you shut up for a moment?!

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:38.190
How the hell can I talk like this?!

00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:39.400
Okay? Okay?
